    "definition": "Exactly21 unit disks, arbitrary unbounded rational centers, maximize positive rational radius of a concentric covered disk. Duplicate centers allowed. Contracting centers and target, then rational approximation, preserves the continuous supremum.",
    "human_source": "Classical Kershner1939 triangular lattice covering method, finite19-site hexagonal patch with2 repeated origins. This local finite-method reconstruction covers7/2; it is not claimed as a separately published21-circle score. Tan2018 reported radius3.804 remains an unreproduced best public value in reviewed Friedman sources.",
    "independent_method": "Root proves ideal scaled triangular tessellation covers the plane with radius999/1000; every omitted site has norm>=scale*sqrt21>7/2+1, so covering sites for the target are retained. Exact rational sqrt3 perturbation error<10^-60 gives retained-center displacement<=2scale*10^-60 and total covering radius<1. Root checks witness equality to this finite formula. Cold/search constructions contain an origin unit disk and haveR1. Formal checker instead enumerates restricted Voronoi vertices and boundary extrema.",
    "audit_scope": "Independent analytic audit covers these admission constructions; other search structures require a separate independent proof before promotion. Formal verifier accepts general rational center layouts and performs full-domain checking.",
    "open_status": "Friedman currently reports21 Tan2018 as Found, with no optimality claim. New2026 proof tags for11..20 do not apply21. Infinite-plane optimal-density theorem is not a finite21 optimality proof.",
    "admission": "Initial/traditional/evolution1, human/reference7/2. All five strict runs, damaged-radius rejection, entire-checker score invariance, analytic independent proof, replay, cold export and all failure controls pass. No sampled-coverage certificate."
  }
